{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1140378-clarifications-concerning-chimeric-reality","id":1140378,"title":"Clarifications concerning chimeric reality","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-09-14T18:12:04-07:00","id":1140378,"title":"Clarifications concerning chimeric reality","content":"So I just read C20 and some my assumptions about chimeric reality were a bit off... I think. So in book one it mentions things like eating actual soup with a chimeric spoon and that people would rationalize this, and that a changeling could fly in a chimeric vehicle but anyone who witnesses this could cause you to crash due to disbelief. However when i looked at rules regarding chimera they didn't seem capable of interacting with the autumn world except in special circumstances like I had originally assumed. Even chimeric weapons cannot cause physical harm.<br /> <br /> My question is: do chimeric items physically exist. The Introduction seems to indicate that they physically exist and cannot be seen by humans while the rules seem to indicate that chimera are a separate state of being with changelings existing in both physical and dream states. And can i know where it states banality can damage chimera, i think i missed that bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3729,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev","user":"Darkfoxdev","date":". 09-15-2017, 12:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev","name":"Darkfoxdev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-14T19:19:58-07:00","id":1140392,"title":"","content":"I usually go with &quot;if no banal creature is looking, the object is real, otherwise it doesnt exist in the mundane world&quot; rule, even knowing it is not an actual rule. But I admit I haven't read the soup part.<br /> <br /> But after reading it, I would go on with &quot;The object doesnt exist in the mundane world, but if it is being use in a way that doesnt bother anyone, and is a simple, regular and monotonous act, banal people will rationalize or just do not notice that it doesnt exist, so it will do it supposed function&quot;. It is about the intent of the use, and the object that is used, and the level of importance people actually put over the use. Seems like a weird ruling for me, but Chimerical Reality vs Mundane Reality always have been one of the most weird aspects of Changeling.<br /> <br /> Also, Changelings do exist in both Mundane and Dream States, but the Dream might affect the Mundane, if nobody is actually against it (if a banal somebody is paying particular attention or it is directly absurd to them). As far as I understood, at least.<br /> <br /> P.S.: I just read the soup stuff now, so take what I said with a grain of salt. I still need to put some more though on it. Just posting it to see if it helps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12934-manbat","name":"Manbat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12934_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-14T19:23:10-07:00","id":1140394,"title":"","content":"Is my (previously house ruled in) ruling to allow for chimerical tunnels in mundane material now canonical? I can't tell from the current examples.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-14T20:49:43-07:00","id":1140418,"title":"","content":"Chimerical creatures require a special Rede called wyrd in order to become solid and interact with the autumn world, and calling on the wyrd makes chimera physical. It looks more and more like they are meant to be non-physical, even chimerical weapons cannot physically harm changelings without calling on the wyrd, i suspect there may have been some miscommunication","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3729,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev","user":"Darkfoxdev","date":". 09-15-2017, 12:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev","name":"Darkfoxdev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-15T03:28:34-07:00","id":1140473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darkfoxdev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1140378-clarifications-concerning-chimeric-reality?p=1140418#post1140418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Chimerical creatures require a special Rede called wyrd in order to become solid and interact with the autumn world, and calling on the wyrd makes chimera physical. It looks more and more like they are meant to be non-physical, even chimerical weapons cannot physically harm changelings without calling on the wyrd, i suspect there may have been some miscommunication</div> </div> </div> </div>It was always like, that.<br /> <br /> The point is that chimerae are as real, as they can get, unless they aren't, which is determined by proximity of non-Dreamer folk. To be more real, they had to have either interact with enchanted people, and to be <i>super-real</i> they have to be Wyrded, one way or another.<br /> <br /> Stealing your eraser gum, while you aren't looking is easier to do, than to appear to you in person and this, in turn, is easier, than break your arm. <br /> <br /> I think, there's a distinct progression here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 09-15-2017, 02:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-16T12:31:02-07:00","id":1140888,"title":"","content":"Unless I'm remembering it wrong, I wrote the Spoon example for &quot;...of the Dreaming's Heart&quot; items. They're not normal chimerical items, but rather Treasures 5 (at least). I chose a spoon because it clearly displays the focus on &quot;intent and belief&quot;, which C20 is bringing out to the front, without making it complicated.<br /> <br /> Also, as you might have noticed, C20 moves away from &quot;Chimerical Reality&quot; and it's now &quot;Chimerical Quality&quot;. Any normal chimerical item has a Quality-appearance and is anchored in a mundane object.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Krister M. Michl</b> <hr /><b>Freelance writer</b> <hr /><a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Krister_M._Michl\" target=\"_blank\">Entry on White Wolf Wikipedia</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2494-rigistrade","name":"Rigistrade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2494_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-16T13:10:57-07:00","id":1140894,"title":"","content":"Okay so basically chimerical items and beings can interact physically when no one it looking, but can't inflict true harm due to banality and/or the mists, since changelings took on mortal form to protect themselves they share this immunity. Am I correct?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev","name":"Darkfoxdev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-16T16:46:28-07:00","id":1140926,"title":"","content":"As far as I know how the rules go, no you are not correct. But that could be a cool house rule.<br /> <br /> As far as understood from the rules, and Registrade explanation, there is 3 kinds of Chimerical Stuff in the Autumn world.<br /> <br /> * Chimerical Quality: The chimerical stuff that has a duality with an Autumn object. A stick, in the Autumn World, that is also a Sword, in his Chimerical Quality. A Tiger Toy that is also a Walking Talking Tiger. Each side affects their respective side (Autumn -&gt; Autumn, Chimerical -&gt; Chimerical) and they dont mix, no matter who is looking. Seems that mostly Chimerical Items fall on this category.<br /> <br /> A Changeling, that is both sides at same time, can affect both ways in different manner, as long as the intent of use is the same. So, if you are changing clothes, your regular Autumn clothes is a T-Shirt and a Jeans, but your Chimerical Clothes are 1600's sweeter with one of those pants that are also socks, your character will change both clothes at same time, even if their Autumn/Chimerical movements are completely different.<br /> <br /> ** Chimera: Purely Chimerical objects, made up of glamour. It has no duality and can only affect the chimerical side of stuff, unless some power changes it (like Calling the Wyrd). It cant affect and is unaffected by the Autumn world. In the Autumn world the Banality will slowly corrode such stuff, if it is not feed up Glamour each once in a while, and the Mists will make people forget any impossible interaction between stuff with Chimerical Qualities and Chimeras. For example, if is there a purely Chimera Horse, and you are riding it, for anyone else you are ridding nothing. Banality might expel it to the Near Dream, while the mists will make people see you running and jumping really fast, or ridding a motorcycle, or just make they unable to identify what you are ridding, or just plainly forget you passed by.<br /> <br /> *** Dream-Heart Treasures: Stuff made up of Glamour that can affect the real world, as long as it follows their intent and no banal people pay a lot of attention.<br /> <br /> Still not quite sure how you create this Dual Quality in Objects, or if you can (and how you do) put a Chimera in a Autumn object in order to have a Chimerical Quality on it, but the book probably has the answer somewhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12934-manbat","name":"Manbat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12934_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-16T17:11:17-07:00","id":1140931,"title":"","content":"Purely chimerical beings can affect the Autumn world, and have been able to in every edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-16T17:11:49-07:00","id":1140932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darkfoxdev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1140378-clarifications-concerning-chimeric-reality?p=1140894#post1140894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay so basically chimerical items and beings can interact physically when no one it looking, but can't inflict true harm due to banality and/or the mists, since changelings took on mortal form to protect themselves they share this immunity. Am I correct?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup, that's right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-16T18:15:58-07:00","id":1140939,"title":"","content":"I just look up and yeah, animate Chimera can actually affect stuff while nobody is looking (even if in another section they say that chimera cannot affect the real world except in special situations), but the book defines as &quot;stealing things or unlocking doors&quot;, but it does not specify the size of the effect. Could a Elephant Chimera just rampantly smashes through a avenue full of cars, as long as no banal creature is looking, or are they limited to small acts?<br /> <br /> And I found no mention that Inanimate Chimera could be used to block a door or hold up the weight of something non-Chimerical, but I think it is fair to extrapolate the rules from the animate chimera to the inanimate. I always thought that it was a house rule, but I guess even a broken clock can be right by accident twice a day.<br /> <br /> But if so, and if I understood right, as long as nobody is looking, I can smash a door with my broomstick that has the Chimerical Axe as his Chimerical Quality, leaving Axe like marks in the door? If yes, why doesnt the axe cause real damage to my fellow Changeling while we fight alone? Is their mortal perception from their mortal eyes that stops the axe from affecting him in the Autumn way? If so, wouldnt my eyes stop my axe from working in the door? Or is it tied to the new Intent and belief functionality somehow?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12934-manbat","name":"Manbat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12934_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-16T20:21:09-07:00","id":1140961,"title":"","content":"one of the other players would like to know if she could keep a forge heated with her chimeric companion (a small dragon), I'm assuming that the answer is yes based on this. I'll admit I used to think chimera existed separate from the physical world similar to twilight in chronicles of darkness. This is...different. Not bad but I could see alot of questions coming in in game (do cameras prevent this, what about ambient banality in a location, what if the subject is unconcious) we might houserule it to only be able to interact in low banality environments","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3729,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev","user":"Darkfoxdev","date":". 09-16-2017, 11:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev","name":"Darkfoxdev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T19:34:30-07:00","id":1141998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darkfoxdev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1140378-clarifications-concerning-chimeric-reality?p=1140961#post1140961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">one of the other players would like to know if she could keep a forge heated with her chimeric companion (a small dragon), I'm assuming that the answer is yes based on this. I'll admit I used to think chimera existed separate from the physical world similar to twilight in chronicles of darkness. This is...different. Not bad but I could see alot of questions coming in in game (do cameras prevent this, what about ambient banality in a location, what if the subject is unconcious) we might houserule it to only be able to interact in low banality environments</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In my games I would allow that chimeric dragon. An unenchanted human wouldn't know that the forge wasn't heated by coal or natural gas if they never saw the dragon, so the Mists wouldn't apply.<br /> <br /> Cameras wouldn't prevent chimera, but wouldn't show them. When the human saw the video or photo, the Mists would affect them similarly to how it would if they saw it in person.<br /> <br /> A chimera belonging to a PC/NPC does have existence outside of that person, even if it originated with them. So unconsciousness shouldn't cause it to even temporarily vanish.<br /> <br /> Ambient banality of a location should affect the chimera's ability to exist or stay in that location.<br /> <br /> That's how I would rule all of this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://imgbb.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://image.ibb.co/fzeOgQ/1172c70f3ff188688852c74c8145285c_original_2_4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> Visit my freehold for Changeling links, settings, art, and other goodies.<br /> <a href=\"https://theshepherdsfreehold.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The Shepherd's Freehold</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13648-shepherd","name":"Shepherd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-25T20:03:37-07:00","id":1143954,"title":"","content":"In previous editions &quot;ambient Banality&quot; and &quot;Banal locations&quot; were not a thing.<br /> Now i think the dragon could work at the forge, as long as it's not a high Banality location (which is unlikely, or you wouldn't have set up shop there). <br /> <br /> As for why the chimerical axe doesn't cause lethal damage to a changeling's mortal self when there are no Banal witnesses... While the chimerical quality is an axe, remember the changeling's chimerical quality is a Troll, and as long as there are no banal witnesses, his Troll self takes precedence, just as the broomstick's &quot;axe-self&quot; does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10198-luisarmander","name":"Luisarmander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}